# Credentials. SPEC.md §10: this file is the bot token, and the bot token is shell access to
# this Mac with permissions bypassed. Committing it once is unrecoverable — it stays in the
# reflog, and on any remote it is simply public. tests/test_layout.py asserts these rules.
.telegram.json
.telegram.json.*
.telegram.json~

# Runtime state: poll offset, lock, listener log, and per-session PTY transcripts. The
# transcripts may quote anything the session saw, which is why the whole tree is ignored
# rather than filtered. SPEC.md §3.
var/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Deliberately NOT `*.log`. tests/fixtures/rc_startup.log is a captured Remote Control startup
# transcript and is what the URL scrape is tested against (SPEC.md §12, slice 6). A blanket log
# rule would drop it from the repo silently; `var/` above already covers every log that is
# actually runtime state.
